<title>ISRAEL: Israel's August trade deficit $1.053 bln.</title>
<headline>Israel's August trade deficit $1.053 bln.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's trade deficit in August totalled $1.053 billion, the Central Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>	     Aug 96    July96     Aug 95</p>
<p>Exports    1,292     1,695	1,266</p>
<p>Imports    2,345     2,552	2,372</p>
<p>Balance   -1,053     - 856     -1,105</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>The bureau said that since March imports have fallen while exports have remained steady. As a result, the trend has been a narrowing of the merchandise trade deficit.</p>
<p>In the first eight months the deficit was $7.478 billion against $6.874 billion a year earlier.</p>
<p>- Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-370-502</p>
</text>
